  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>As the given capacitors are in parallel combination, therefore,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math></p><p>Hence, charge flown through the switch<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
